  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "What is the value of the following expression?\n\n\\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{2}{10} + \\frac{3}{10} + \\frac{4}{10} \\\\ &\\quad {}+ \\frac{5}{10} + \\frac{6}{10} + \\frac{7}{10} + \\frac{8}{10} \\\\ &\\quad {}+ \\frac{9}{10} + \\frac{55}{10} \\end{aligned} \\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(4\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)",
    "B": "\\(6.4\\)",
    "C": "\\(9\\)",
    "D": "\\(10\\)",
    "E": "\\(11\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Every term is measured in tenths, so add the numerators and keep the denominator \\(10\\). Pairing the smaller numerators makes their sum quick to find:\n\\[\n(1+9)+(2+8)+(3+7)+(4+6)+5=45.\n\\]\nTherefore the expression equals\n\\[\n\\frac{45+55}{10}=\\frac{100}{10}=10.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{10}\\), choice D.",
